---
import DownloadButtons from '../../components/DownloadButtons.astro'
import Page from '../../layouts/Page.astro';
---

<Page
  title="AI Presentation Generator: outline first, then paint | Oia"
  description="Generate multi-page presentations with AI: review the page outline before a single image is spent, export to PDF or PPTX. Free, open source, bring your own provider."
  ogTitle="AI Presentation Generator: outline first | Oia"
  ogDescription="Review the outline before a single image is spent. Export PDF &amp; PPTX."
  canonical="https://oia.solutions/use-cases/presentations/"
  base="../../"
  links={[{ href: '../../#workflow', label: 'How it works' }, { href: '../../prompts/', label: 'Prompt library' }, { href: '../../templates/', label: 'Templates' }]}
  footerLinks={[{ href: '../../', label: 'Home' }, { href: '../../prompts/', label: 'Prompt library' }, { href: '../../templates/', label: 'Templates' }, { href: '../flash-sale-banners/', label: 'Flash-sale banners' }, { href: '../livestream-overlays/', label: 'Livestream overlays' }]}
>
<header class="pageHero">
  <p class="kicker">Use case, decks</p>
  <h1>Decks that plan themselves, and wait for your yes.</h1>
  <p class="lede">Ask for a pitch deck and Oia stops at the outline first: page titles and summaries you can rewrite before a single image is spent. Then every page is painted in one consistent style, editable on a real canvas, exportable to PDF and PPTX.</p>
  <DownloadButtons rowClass="ctaRow" anchorId="download" installHref="../../install/" ghost={{ href: '../../prompts/', label: 'Copy the prompts' }} />
</header>

<main class="pageMain">
  <p class="catNote">Open the desktop app to preview presentation templates, plan pages as an outline, and export your deck.</p>

  <div class="ucGrid">
    <div>
      <h2 class="catH" style="margin-top:8px">The outline gate</h2>
      <div class="stepsList">
        <div><span class="n">01: ASK</span><h3>One prompt, N pages</h3><p>"An 8-page product-launch deck for a skincare serum": set pages 3-9 in the composer.</p></div>
        <div><span class="n">02: REVIEW</span><h3>Outline first, zero images</h3><p>The deck stops at an outline card: rewrite any page title or summary before painting. Outline edits are free.</p></div>
        <div><span class="n">03: PAINT</span><h3>One style across pages</h3><p>Every page generates from the same plan and brand kit: consistent palette, layout and type.</p></div>
        <div><span class="n">04: EXPORT</span><h3>PDF &amp; PPTX</h3><p>PDF preserves mixed page sizes; PPTX puts each page on a slide. Edit any page on the canvas before you ship.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h2 class="catH" style="margin-top:8px">Why it's different</h2>
      <div class="promptGrid">
        <div class="promptCard"><h3>No surprise 30-slide bills</h3><p class="mono" style="font-size:11px;color:var(--muted)">The outline is the contract: page count is locked before a single image is spent.</p></div>
        <div class="promptCard"><h3>Real pages, real edits</h3><p class="mono" style="font-size:11px;color:var(--muted)">Each page is a canvas: move the headline, restyle a chart card, duplicate a page for the next chapter.</p></div>
        <div class="promptCard"><h3>Brand kit on every page</h3><p class="mono" style="font-size:11px;color:var(--muted)">Palette and guidance ride the whole deck, not just page one.</p></div>
        <div class="promptCard"><h3>Your quota, your rules</h3><p class="mono" style="font-size:11px;color:var(--muted)">≈ N images shown up front, a daily counter in the sidebar. No credits, no subscription.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq" style="margin-top:26px">
        <details><summary>Can I review the deck before images are generated?</summary><p>Yes, multi-page requests stop at an outline card first: page titles and summaries you can rewrite before anything is painted. Outline edits cost zero images.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Can I export to PowerPoint?</summary><p>Yes, PPTX places each rendered page on a slide, and PDF preserves mixed page sizes. Canvas text layers are not converted into native PowerPoint text boxes.</p></details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</main>
</Page>
